 ## How it works
-The method operates on a set of particles or a voxel grid, rendering them as a series of slices perpendicular to a calculated half-angle vector. It requires two render targets: an **Eye Buffer** (accumulating the final image) and a **Light Buffer** (storing transmittance/attenuation). The Light Buffer must include an alpha channel to store accumulated opacity for the "under" blending operator [S2, unofficial].
